      "frameId": null,
      "updated": 1789925713457,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "id": "el067",
      "x": 94,
      "y": 1003.75,
      "width": 1262,
      "height": 162.5,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "seed": 1338439845,
      "versionNonce": 649152057,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "TRAPS  (each one cost a build or a boot)\n\n\u2022  entry 1 \"trapp-os (manual)\" has NO install-mode - picking it boots live and installs nothing.\n   That is why cp-01 sat idle for 14 h with an untouched disk.\n\u2022  docker here is the SNAP build: a /tmp bind mount silently mounts EMPTY inside the container.\n   Anything docker must read lives under $HOME. build.sh stages into artifacts/staging/.\n\u2022  the rootfs overlay hides inside rootfs.squashfs - an ISO listing will not show a missing banner.\n   build.sh unsquashes and compares it on every build.\n\u2022  /etc is an overlay on tmpfs; only /oem, /usr/local, /home and declared binds survive a reboot.\n\u2022  never put the CD before the disk in boot_order with install.auto - that is an endless wipe loop.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "el066",
      "originalText": "TRAPS  (each one cost a build or a boot)\n\n\u2022  entry 1 \"trapp-os (manual)\" has NO install-mode - picking it boots live and installs nothing.\n   That is why cp-01 sat idle for 14 h with an untouched disk.\n\u2022  docker here is the SNAP build: a /tmp bind mount silently mounts EMPTY inside the container.\n   Anything docker must read lives under $HOME. build.sh stages into artifacts/staging/.\n\u2022  the rootfs overlay hides inside rootfs.squashfs - an ISO listing will not show a missing banner.\n   build.sh unsquashes and compares it on every build.\n\u2022  /etc is an overlay on tmpfs; only /oem, /usr/local, /home and declared binds survive a reboot.\n\u2022  never put the CD before the disk in boot_order with install.auto - that is an endless wipe loop.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
